0kohaerenzprotokoll.scripts.account.account_orderaccount_orderŒDoes the pipeline's dependency order hold, per document?

    The steps have an order ‚Äî extract before reconcile, and each reconciliation
    against the state the previous one left. Nothing enforced it, and it broke:
    document 4 was first reconciled against 14 pages, the state document 1 left,
    while document 3 had already taken it to 24.

    Borrowed from the RLM-workflow skill's `validate_dag`, whose point is that the
    ordering is plain Python and must never be left to judgement: it will be wrong
    on the day it matters. Here the order is checked rather than assumed. Ç(—8Bc2ec09744601f1e9HƒR07f24fd1d7cb8561R2088e1e7bb31e1e1R209607b0147aaef6R2bba36cf21007aebR2c5e7f7c8af801f6R2ec665ee2847daeaR329bd1684f0be72eR3f48d87d6505d7a0R464c472748c9dcb7R4dfb322278b1d792R4ffa9375f0438138R520649e17fb5295dR5839ecc56eb7a9d2R67410974297a3c3fR73bec7d4ea5355a7R89283a0af236989dR8a76b7690e477b05R97dd93249a5108efRa636de7a7ce6121cRaf29c4c22e683defRb4f4e4d3c978dfbdRbd19fe9edcb77e1bRc265735eec8d3e0bRd1a259572cdb5171Rd656fa6b9102e19fRd7faf366ed6a3e22Re1152aa3c2e94a95Rf32c537fc583278fRfed8a30ad056cd8cRff068fd422ec73dfZdict
